# Citation File Format（https://citation-file-format.github.io/）
cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "PaperGate: a deterministic, check-gated framework for academic writing"
message: "If you use PaperGate in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  PaperGate turns the non-deterministic parts of academic writing into deterministic,
  machine-checked rules. The checks ask whether the manuscript, the bibliography, the
  reading notes and the analysis outputs agree with each other, while the paper's
  history in git supplies the traceability a review process needs. Standards state what
  counts as correct, the check command executes them, and skills wrap the literature
  and export tooling.
keywords:
  - academic writing
  - reproducibility
  - citation audit
  - research workflow
  - git
authors:
  - name: "ls-open"
    website: "https://github.com/ls-open"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ls-open/papergate"
